ices\n\n5. **Veterans Benefits** (if applicable — should be screened):\n   - VA Aid and Attendance benefit: Up to \$2,431/month for veterans needing assistance with ADLs\n   - VA caregiver support program\n\n6. **Long-Term Care Planning**:\n   - If the patient does not have long-term care insurance, Medicaid planning with an elder law attorney may be necessary to protect the wife\'s assets while qualifying the patient for Medicaid nursing facility coverage\n   - **Spousal impoverishment protection**: Federal law protects the community spouse (the wife) from losing all assets when the other spouse qualifies for Medicaid — she is entitled to retain a minimum monthly maintenance needs allowance and a community spouse resource allowance\n\n7. **Emergency Resources**:\n   - If the wife\'s health deteriorates acutely, the patient can be placed in an **emergency respite** through CPS/Adult Protective Services or through hospital social work emergency protocols\n   - If the wife is hospitalized, the patient would need immediate temporary placement — having this plan in place before a crisis is essential',
